42.4,"debt_to_ebitda":9.5,"net_debt_to_ebitda":-4.85,"f_score":6,"f_score_breakdown":[{"id":1,"category":"盈利能力","desc":"資產回報率 ROA > 0","passed":1,"detail":"當期 ROA = 30.3%"},{"id":2,"category":"盈利能力","desc":"營業現金流 CFO > 0","passed":1,"detail":"自由現金流 = $1,162M"},{"id":3,"category":"盈利能力","desc":"資產回報率持續擴張 (ΔROA > 0)","passed":1,"detail":"回報率穩步領先同業基準"},{"id":4,"category":"盈利能力","desc":"應計利潤品質高 (CFO > 淨利潤)","passed":0,"detail":"真實現金流充沛，無虛報帳面獲利"},{"id":5,"category":"槓桿與償債","desc":"財務槓桿未惡化 (ΔLeverage ≤ 0)","passed":0,"detail":"總負債資產比率 = 67.9%"},{"id":6,"category":"槓桿與償債","desc":"短期流動性安全 (ΔLiquidity > 0)","passed":0,"detail":"流動比率 = 0.60"},{"id":7,"category":"槓桿與償債","desc":"股本未遭稀釋 (ΔShares ≤ 0)","passed":1,"detail":"未大幅增發新股割韭菜"},{"id":8,"category":"營運效率","desc":"毛利率擴張 (ΔMargin > 0)","passed":1,"detail":"產品定價權增強，毛利結構健康"},{"id":9,"category":"營運效率","desc":"資產週轉率提升 (ΔTurnover > 0)","passed":1,"detail":"每單位資產產出效益改善"}],"fair_val":36.05,"default_fair_val":36.05,"premium_pct":-53.9,"is_undervalued":true,"pe_trailing":2.2,"pe_forward":1.9,"pb_trailing":2.1,"pb_forward":1.9,"div_yield":0,"ps_ratio":1.3,"fcf_to_ev":20.64,"fcf_to_mcap":18.52,"liab_to_assets":67.9,"cash_to_assets":20.5,"current_ratio":0.6,"roe":94.3,"roa":30.3,"moat":{"ticker":"LYFT","period":"2026Q3","m1_brand_pricing":{"score":6,"comment_zh":"Lyft 的品牌在美國叫車市場具有一定的知名度，但與 Uber 相比，其品牌影響力相對較弱。定價策略上，Lyft 經常需要與 Uber 進行價格競爭，尤其是在促銷和折扣方面，這削弱了其定價權。雖然 Lyft 努力建立差異化形象，例如強調司機福利和社區感，但這些努力尚未轉化為顯著的品牌溢價或客戶忠誠度。其品牌價值更多體現在市場份額的爭奪上，而非獨立的定價能力。","comment_en":"Lyft's brand has some recognition in the US ride-sharing market, but its influence is relatively weaker compared to Uber. In terms of pricing strategy, Lyft often engages in price competition with Uber, especially concerning promotions and discounts, which weakens its pricing power. Although Lyft strives to build a differentiated image, emphasizing driver welfare and community, these efforts have not yet translated into significant brand premiums or customer loyalty. Its brand value is more reflected in market share battles rather than independent pricing capability."},"m2_patents_regulatory":{"score":2,"comment_zh":"叫車服務行業的進入壁壘主要來自監管和牌照，而非技術專利。Lyft 在專利方面幾乎沒有顯著的競爭優勢。其業務高度依賴於各地的監管環境，包括司機分類、安全標準和營運許可。監管的變化可能對其營運模式和成本結構產生重大影響。雖然 Lyft 積極參與政策制定，但這更多是應對外部風險，而非建立可持續的專利壁壘。","comment_en":"The barriers to entry in the ride-sharing industry stem primarily from regulation and licensing, rather than technological patents. Lyft possesses virtually no significant competitive advantage in terms of patents. Its business is highly dependent on the regulatory environment in various locations, including driver classification, safety standards, and operating permits. Changes in regulation can significantly impact its operating model and cost structure. While Lyft actively participates in policy-making, this is more about managing external risks than establishing sustainable patent barriers."},"m3_high_switching_costs":{"score":4,"comment_zh":"對於乘客而言，從 Lyft 轉換到其他叫車平台（如 Uber）的轉換成本非常低。用戶只需下載另一個應用程式，且通常可以利用新用戶優惠。雖然 Lyft 透過會員計畫（如 Lyft Pink）試圖增加客戶黏性，但其效果有限。對於司機而言，轉換平台也相對容易，他們可以同時在多個平台營運。因此，客戶轉換成本不高，這使得 Lyft 難以鎖定用戶。","comment_en":"For passengers, the switching costs from Lyft to other ride-sharing platforms like Uber are very low. Users only need to download another app and can often take advantage of new user discounts. While Lyft attempts to increase customer stickiness through membership programs (like Lyft Pink), their effectiveness is limited. For drivers, switching platforms is also relatively easy, and they can operate on multiple platforms simultaneously. Therefore, customer switching costs are not high, making it difficult for Lyft to lock in users."},"m4_network_effects":{"score":8,"comment_zh":"叫車服務的網絡效應是其核心競爭力之一。更多的乘客吸引更多的司機，從而縮短等待時間並提高服務可用性；更多的司機則能更好地滿足乘客需求，形成正向循環。Lyft 在美國和加拿大的主要城市建立了相當規模的用戶基礎，這使得新進入者難以複製其網絡效應。儘管 Uber 在全球範圍內擁有更強的網絡效應，但在 Lyft 專注的市場，其網絡效應仍然是重要的壁壘。","comment_en":"The network effect is one of the core competitive strengths of ride-sharing services. More passengers attract more drivers, thereby reducing wait times and increasing service availability; more drivers can better meet passenger demand, forming a virtuous cycle. Lyft has established a considerable user base in major cities across the US and Canada, making it difficult for new entrants to replicate its network effects. Although Uber has stronger network effects globally, in the markets Lyft focuses on, its network effects remain a significant barrier."},"m5_cost_advantage_scale":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"Lyft 作為美國第二大叫車平台，在規模經濟方面具有顯著優勢。其龐大的用戶基礎和司機網絡使其能夠更有效地分攤固定成本，如技術開發、市場營銷和客戶服務。與小型競爭對手相比，Lyft 在獲取用戶和司機方面的邊際成本可能更低。此外，隨著自動駕駛技術的發展，規模優勢在未來可能進一步放大，尤其是在車隊管理和營運效率方面。","comment_en":"As the second-largest ride-sharing platform in the US, Lyft possesses a significant advantage in economies of scale. Its large user base and driver network enable it to spread fixed costs, such as technology development, marketing, and customer service, more efficiently. Compared to smaller competitors, Lyft's marginal cost of acquiring users and drivers may be lower. Furthermore, with the development of autonomous driving technology, the scale advantage may be further amplified in the future, especially in fleet management and operational efficiency."},"m6_unique_geography_assets":{"score":3,"comment_zh":"Lyft 的業務模式高度標準化，主要集中在北美地區的城市市場。它不擁有獨特的地理資產或特許經營權，其營運地點與競爭對手高度重疊。雖然在某些特定城市 Lyft 可能擁有較強的市場份額，但這更多是網絡效應的體現，而非基於獨特的地理位置或資源。其業務的同質性使得它難以建立基於地理位置的獨特壁壘。","comment_en":"Lyft's business model is highly standardized, primarily focused on urban markets in North America. It does not own unique geographical assets or franchises, and its operating locations heavily overlap with competitors. While Lyft may hold a stronger market share in certain specific cities, this is more a reflection of network effects rather than being based on unique geographical locations or resources. The homogeneity of its business makes it difficult to establish unique barriers based on geography."},"m7_operational_efficiency":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"Lyft 在過去幾年持續追求營運效率的提升，尤其是在優化司機匹配、路線規劃和減少空駛率方面。公司透過數據分析和演算法不斷改進其平台效率。儘管與 Uber 相比，其整體營運規模較小，但在其專注的市場，Lyft 已經達到了相當高的營運效率水平。近期財報顯示其已實現盈利，這證明了其在成本控制和營運優化方面的努力已見成效。","comment_en":"Lyft has continuously pursued improvements in operational efficiency over the past few years, particularly in optimizing driver matching, route planning, and reducing idle mileage. The company constantly enhances its platform efficiency through data analysis and algorithms. Although its overall operational scale is smaller compared to Uber, Lyft has achieved a considerable level of operational efficiency in the markets it focuses on. Recent financial reports indicate profitability, demonstrating the effectiveness of its efforts in cost control and operational optimization."},"m8_capital_allocation":{"score":6,"comment_zh":"Lyft 的資本配置策略在過去幾年經歷了顯著轉變。從早期追求市場份額增長，轉向更注重盈利能力和自由現金流。公司在自動駕駛技術研發和市場擴張上的投入相對謹慎，並開始回購股票。然而，相較於一些擁有強大自由現金流並持續進行價值投資的公司，Lyft 的資本配置能力仍有提升空間，尤其是在如何最大化股東回報方面。","comment_en":"Lyft's capital allocation strategy has undergone a significant shift in recent years, moving from an early focus on market share growth to emphasizing profitability and free cash flow. The company's investments in autonomous driving technology R&D and market expansion have been relatively cautious, and it has begun share buybacks. However, compared to some companies with strong free cash flow that consistently engage in value investing, Lyft's capital allocation capabilities still have room for improvement, particularly in maximizing shareholder returns."},"m9_customer_retention":{"score":5,"comment_zh":"Lyft 的客戶留存率面臨挑戰，主要原因是行業競爭激烈以及用戶轉換成本低。雖然 Lyft Pink 等會員計畫旨在提高客戶忠誠度，但其吸引力和留存效果仍有待加強。用戶可能會因為價格、可用性或促銷活動而頻繁切換平台。要顯著提高客戶留存率，Lyft 需要提供更獨特的價值主張或更強的差異化服務，以區別於競爭對手。","comment_en":"Lyft's customer retention rate faces challenges, primarily due to intense industry competition and low user switching costs. While membership programs like Lyft Pink aim to enhance customer loyalty, their attractiveness and retention effectiveness still need strengthening. Users may frequently switch platforms due to price, availability, or promotional offers. To significantly improve customer retention, Lyft needs to offer a more unique value proposition or more differentiated services to stand out from competitors."},"m10_durability":{"score":5,"comment_zh":"Lyft 的業務模式在短期內具有一定的可持續性，尤其是在其核心市場。然而，其長期耐久性面臨來自技術變革（如自動駕駛的普及）、監管風險以及持續激烈的市場競爭的挑戰。如果自動駕駛技術能夠廣泛應用並降低營運成本，現有的叫車平台模式可能會受到顛覆。因此，Lyft 的長期護城河相對較弱，其未來成功很大程度上取決於其適應和轉型的能力。","comment_en":"Lyft's business model possesses a certain degree of sustainability in the short term, especially in its core markets. However, its long-term durability faces challenges from technological changes (such as the widespread adoption of autonomous driving), regulatory risks, and ongoing intense market competition. If autonomous driving technology becomes widely adopted and reduces operational costs, the existing ride-sharing platform model could be disrupted. Therefore, Lyft's long-term moat is relatively weak, and its future success largely depends on its ability to adapt and transform."},"overall_moat_verdict_zh":"Lyft 的經濟護城河主要建立在網絡效應和規模經濟之上，這使其在北美叫車市場具有一定的競爭優勢。然而，其品牌定價權、客戶轉換成本和專利壁壘相對較弱，且業務易受監管變化影響。雖然公司在營運效率和資本配置上有所改進，但其長期耐久性面臨自動駕駛技術和激烈競爭的挑戰。總體而言，Lyft 的護城河屬於「商品型」服務的範疇，依賴於網絡效應的維持，而非難以複製的獨特資產或強大品牌溢價。","overall_moat_verdict_en":"Lyft's economic moat is primarily built on network effects and economies of scale, granting it a certain competitive advantage in the North American ride-sharing market. However, its brand pricing power, customer switching costs, and patent barriers are relatively weak, and its business is susceptible to regulatory changes. While the company has improved operational efficiency and capital allocation, its long-term durability faces challenges from autonomous driving technology and intense competition. Overall, Lyft's moat falls into the category of a 'commodity-like' service, relying on the maintenance of network effects rather than on irreplicable unique assets or strong brand premiums.","evidenceHash":"a7d49145cdfe7fadb4df7c0d2a6c84b5cc8eb0f266fb3ee5dd25ae555064e675","assessmentPolicy":"buffett-moat-v3","model":"gemini-2.5-flash-lite","provider":"Gemini"},"ratingSources":{"moat":{"reason":null,"evidenceHash":"a7d49145cdfe7fadb4df7c0d2a6c84b5cc8eb0f266fb3ee5dd25ae555064e675","currentEvidenceHash":"a7d49145cdfe7fadb4df7c0d2a6c84b5cc8eb0f266fb3ee5dd25ae555064e675"},"fScore":{"score":6,"checkedAt":null},"zScore":{"asOfDate":"2025-12-31","period":"FY 2025","basis":"comparableAnnual","model":"z","zone":"distress","reason":null,"scoringCurrency":"USD","applicability":null,"checkedAt":"2026-11-13T07:50:24.576Z","evidenceHash":"1ead07606f11b8ad972cac50713f025b7094c8b974b362280178b6f7dfdc875e"},"mScore":{"asOfDate":"2024-12-31","period":"FY 2024","basis":"comparableAnnual","model":null,"zone":"clean","reason":null,"scoringCurrency":"USD","applicability":null,"checkedAt":"2026-11-13T07:50:24.576Z","evidenceHash":"1ead07606f11b8ad972cac50713f025b7094c8b974b362280178b6f7dfdc875e"}},"fin_valuation":{"is_financial":false},"image":"https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/LYFT.png","logo":"https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/LYFT.png","website":"https://www.lyft.com","ceo":"John David Risher","full_time_employees":"3913","description":"Lyft, Inc. facilitates a comprehensive, on-demand transportation platform spanning the United States and Canada. Its core mission involves offering users personalized and immediate access to diverse mobility solutions through its multimodal network. Among its primary services is the Ridesharing Marketplace, which seamlessly connects drivers with passengers. For drivers, the company provides Express Drive, a flexible program for vehicle rentals. Consumers can also utilize Lyft Rentals for longer-distance travel needs. Furthermore, in numerous urban centers, Lyft operates a fleet of shared bikes and scooters, ideal for shorter journeys. The Lyft app enhances its utility by incorporating public transit data, thereby expanding the array of available transport options for users. Beyond these offerings, the company also provides access to autonomous vehicles, specialized enterprise transportation solutions (including concierge services for organizations), and subscription benefits through its Lyft Pink plans. Additional services include Lyft Pass commuter programs, first-mile and last-mile connectivity, and university safe rides initiatives. Established in 2007, the company initially operated as Zimride, Inc. before officially rebranding to Lyft, Inc. in April 2013. Its corporate headquarters are located in San Francisco, California.","description_en":"Lyft, Inc. facilitates a comprehensive, on-demand transportation platform spanning the United States and Canada. Its core mission involves offering users personalized and immediate access to diverse mobility solutions through its multimodal network. Among its primary services is the Ridesharing Marketplace, which seamlessly connects drivers with passengers. For drivers, the company provides Express Drive, a flexible program for vehicle rentals. Consumers can also utilize Lyft Rentals for longer-distance travel needs. Furthermore, in numerous urban centers, Lyft operates a fleet of shared bikes and scooters, ideal for shorter journeys. The Lyft app enhances its utility by incorporating public transit data, thereby expanding the array of available transport options for users. Beyond these offerings, the company also provides access to autonomous vehicles, specialized enterprise transportation solutions (including concierge services for organizations), and subscription benefits through its Lyft Pink plans. Additional services include Lyft Pass commuter programs, first-mile and last-mile connectivity, and university safe rides initiatives. Established in 2007, the company initially operated as Zimride, Inc. before officially rebranding to Lyft, Inc. in April 2013. Its corporate headquarters are located in San Francisco, California.","description_zh":"Lyft, Inc.（美股代碼：LYFT）為 Technology 領域之重要企業，專注於 Software - Application 業務，具備清晰之商業壁壘與現金流創造能力。","address":"185 Berry Street","city":"San Francisco","state":"CA","zip":"94107","country":"US","phone":"844 250 2773","full_address":"185 Berry Street, San Francisco, CA 94107, US","range_52w":"12.46-24.59","year_high":24.59,"year_low":12.46,"all_time_high":0,"all_time_low":12.46,"inst_ownership_pct":null,"insider_ownership_pct":null,"top_holders":[],"insider_trades":[{"date":"2026-10-22","name":"Whiteside Janey","title":"director","is_buy":null,"action":"A-Award","shares":775,"price":0,"total_val":0},{"date":"2026-10-22","name":"Stephenson Dave","title":"director","is_buy":null,"action":"A-Award","shares":942,"price":0,"total_val":0},{"date":"2026-10-22","name":"Brous Michael Zachary","title":"officer: CHIEF FINANCIAL OFFICER","is_buy":null,"action":"A-Award","shares":80561,"price":0,"total_val":0},{"date":"2026-10-22","name":"Brous Michael Zachary","title":"officer: CHIEF FINANCIAL OFFICER","is_buy":null,"action":"A-Award","shares":48958,"price":0,"total_val":0},{"date":"2026-10-22","name":"Brous Michael Zachary","title":"officer: CHIEF FINANCIAL OFFICER","is_buy":null,"action":"A-Award","shares":126342,"price":0,"total_val":0},{"date":"2026-10-02","name":"Brous Michael Zachary","title":"officer: CHIEF FINANCIAL OFFICER","is_buy":null,"action":"","shares":0,"price":0,"total_val":0},{"date":"2026-09-25","name":"Brewer Erin","title":"officer: CHIEF FINANCIAL OFFICER","is_buy":false,"action":"S-Sale","shares":15000,"price":14.64,"total_val":0.22},{"date":"2026-09-03","name":"Llewellyn Lindsay Catherine","title":"officer: SEE REMARKS","is_buy":false,"action":"S-Sale","shares":13204,"price":16.64,"total_val":0.22},{"date":"2026-08-31","name":"Lawee David","title":"director","is_buy":false,"action":"S-Sale","shares":4613,"price":17.33,"total_val":0.08},{"date":"2026-08-31","name":"Hope Stephen W.","title